The package installs headers under:
  include/keyhcommon/commonbase
  include/keyhcommon/reflectsystem
  include/keyhcommon/appsystem

CMake usage:
  find_package(KeyhCommon CONFIG REQUIRED)
  target_link_libraries(your-target PRIVATE KeyhCommon::KeyhCommon)

To link individual libraries instead:
  target_link_libraries(your-target PRIVATE
      KeyhCommon::CommonBase
      KeyhCommon::ReflectSystem
      KeyhCommon::AppSystem)

For MSBuild consumers using vcpkg integration, add the required libraries to
AdditionalDependencies:
  CommonBase.lib;ReflectSystem.lib;AppSystem.lib

Reflection code generation tools are installed alongside the matching library:
  tools/keyhcommon/reflect_codegen.py
  tools/keyhcommon/run_reflect_codegen.bat

Python 3 is not bundled with the package. The wrapper tries py -3, python, then
python3 and verifies the interpreter. To select a specific installation, set
KEYHCOMMON_PYTHON to its executable path (without surrounding quotes):
  set "KEYHCOMMON_PYTHON=C:\Program Files\Python313\python.exe"
This override is authoritative; an invalid override fails instead of falling back.
For MSBuild consumers, replace the old project-local generator in the pre-build
event with the installed wrapper (after vcpkg has installed the package):
  call "$(KeyhCommonInstalledTripletDir)\tools\keyhcommon\run_reflect_codegen.bat" "$(ProjectDir)."
Define KeyhCommonInstalledTripletDir as an absolute path to the installed triplet
directory, for example C:\path\to\KeyhEngine\vcpkg_installed\x64-windows for a
manifest install, or C:\path\to\vcpkg\installed\x64-windows for a classic install.
Use the triplet and installation root actually selected by your build. This is
a consumer-defined property, not one automatically supplied by vcpkg.
The first argument is the directory containing the headers to scan. An optional
second argument selects a shared output directory. Without it, each generated
.inl is placed next to its source header, including headers in subdirectories.
This now matches the Python CLI; pass the first argument again as the second
argument to retain the old wrapper's single-output-directory behavior. When using
a shared output directory, add it to the compiler's include paths and ensure
header base names are unique.

The wrapper resolves reflect_codegen.py beside itself, not from the current
working directory or SolutionDir. No KeyhCommon source checkout is required.
Keep both installed files together. Batch files are packaged as ASCII with CRLF
line endings for cmd.exe, independently of Git checkout settings.
In Visual Studio's pre-build event editor, enter the call command directly.
Do not paste the batch file's contents into the event. Keep call so MSBuild's
event script continues, and propagate failure before running further commands:
  if errorlevel 1 exit /b %errorlevel%

CMake consumers can use KeyhCommon_TOOLS_DIR and KeyhCommon_REFLECT_CODEGEN
after find_package(KeyhCommon CONFIG REQUIRED). For example:
  find_package(Python3 REQUIRED COMPONENTS Interpreter)
  add_custom_target(your-reflection-codegen
      COMMAND "${Python3_EXECUTABLE}" "${KeyhCommon_REFLECT_CODEGEN}"
          --project-dir "${CMAKE_CURRENT_SOURCE_DIR}"
      VERBATIM)
  add_dependencies(your-target your-reflection-codegen)
Without --output-dir, the Python script writes each .inl next to its header.
The generator updates generated #include directives in the source headers.
It skips vcpkg_installed, .git, and .vs subdirectories. Point --project-dir at
your own source tree, not the installed package; use a narrow source directory
if dependencies are installed under another name or location.

When switching from an older generator, remove its generated reflection .inl
files and regenerate them with the packaged tool before compiling. Replace all
old generator invocations so they cannot overwrite the new output.
The package does not automatically enable code generation in consumer projects.
Registry publication scripts, tests, and Python caches are not installed.

To use this repository as a custom registry, add it to your
vcpkg-configuration.json and declare "keyhcommon" in your project's
vcpkg.json dependencies.
